-- title:
--   Completed fundamental identity: prod_{v∈ S}#(mathcal Oᵥ/pmathcal Oᵥ)=p^{[K:ℚ]}
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field (a field of characteristic zero, finite-dimensional over $\mathbb Q$, with ring of integers $\mathcal O_K$ written `NumberField.RingOfIntegers K`), let $p$ be a prime natural number, and let $S$ be a finite set of points of the height-one spectrum of $\mathcal O_K$, i.e. of nonzero prime ideals $v$ with underlying ideal `v.asIdeal`. Assume that $S$ contains every $v$ whose ideal contains the image of $p$ in $\mathcal O_K$, that is, every finite place of $K$ above $p$. For each $v$, let $\mathcal O_v$ denote `v.adicCompletionIntegers K`, the valuation ring of the $v$-adic completion $K_v$, and consider the quotient of $\mathcal O_v$ by the principal ideal generated by the image of $p$ in $\mathcal O_v$. The theorem asserts that the product over $v \in S$ of the cardinalities (as natural numbers, via `Nat.card`) of these quotients equals $p^{\dim_{\mathbb Q} K}$, the $[K:\mathbb Q]$-th power of $p$. Places of $S$ not above $p$ are permitted and contribute a factor $1$, since there $p$ is a unit of $\mathcal O_v$.
--
--   This is the fundamental identity $\sum_{v\mid p} e_v f_v = [K:\mathbb Q]$ in multiplicative form, transferred to the completions: the index of $p\mathcal O_v$ in $\mathcal O_v$ is $p^{e_v f_v}$. It feeds the local counting arguments used in the Selmer-group and class-number computations, being cited in the determination of $\#(\mathcal O_v/p\mathcal O_v)$ for $K = \mathbb Q$ and in the global product formula for indices of $p$-th power subgroups of local unit groups.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_NumberField_prod_natCard_adicCompletionIntegers_quotient_span_natCast_eq_pow_finrank.lean

